{"surah": 63, "verses": [{"ayah": 1, "text": "إِذَا جَآءَكَ ٱلْمُنَٰفِقُونَ قَالُوا۟ نَشْهَدُ إِنَّكَ لَرَسُولُ ٱللَّهِۗ وَٱللَّهُ يَعْلَمُ إِنَّكَ لَرَسُولُهُۥ وَٱللَّهُ يَشْهَدُ إِنَّ ٱلْمُنَٰفِقِينَ لَكَٰذِبُونَ ", "translation": "When the hypocrites come to you, [O Muḥammad], they say, \"We testify that you are the Messenger of Allāh.\" And Allāh knows that you are His Messenger, and Allāh testifies that the hypocrites are liars.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِذَا", "translit": "āَhdِiʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "idhā"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "جَآءَكَ", "translit": "َkَءٓāَjg", "root": "جيا", "latinTranslit": "jāaka"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلْمُنَٰفِقُونَ", "translit": "َnwُqِfَٰnُmْlٱ", "root": "نفق", "latinTranslit": "l-munāfiqūna"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "قَالُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlāَq", "root": "قول", "latinTranslit": "qālū"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "نَشْهَدُ", "translit": "ُdَhْhsَn", "root": "شهد", "latinTranslit": "nashhadu"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "إِنَّكَ", "translit": "َkَّnِiʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "innaka"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "لَرَسُولُ", "translit": "ُlwُsَrَl", "root": "رسل", "latinTranslit": "larasūlu"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله", "latinTranslit": "l-lahi"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "وَٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱَw", "root": "اله", "latinTranslit": "wal-lahu"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "يَعْلَمُ", "translit": "ُmَlْعَy", "root": "علم", "latinTranslit": "yaʿlamu"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "إِنَّكَ", "translit": "َkَّnِiʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "innaka"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "لَرَسُولُهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhُlwُsَrَl", "root": "رسل", "latinTranslit": "larasūluhu"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "وَٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱَw", "root": "اله", "latinTranslit": "wal-lahu"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "يَشْهَدُ", "translit": "ُdَhْhsَy", "root": "شهد", "latinTranslit": "yashhadu"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "إِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "inna"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "ٱلْمُنَٰفِقِينَ", "translit": "َnyِqِfَٰnُmْlٱ", "root": "نفق", "latinTranslit": "l-munāfiqīna"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "لَكَٰذِبُونَ", "translit": "َnwُbِhdَٰkَl", "root": "كذب", "latinTranslit": "lakādhibūna"}], "hasIhya": true, "haleemTranslation": "When the hypocrites come to you [Prophet], they say, ‘We bear witness that you are the Messenger of God.’ God knows that you truly are His Messenger and He bears witness that the hypocrites are liars––", "clearyTranslation": "When the hypocrites come to you [Prophet], they say, ‘We bear witness that you are the Messenger of God.’ God knows that you truly are His Messenger and He bears witness that the hypocrites are liars––"}, {"ayah": 2, "text": "ٱتَّخَذُوٓا۟ أَيْمَٰنَهُمْ جُنَّةً فَصَدُّوا۟ عَن سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِۚ إِنَّهُمْ سَآءَ مَا كَانُوا۟ يَعْمَلُونَ ", "translation": "They have taken their oaths as a cover, so they averted [people] from the way of Allāh. Indeed, it was evil that they were doing.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "ٱتَّخَذُوٓا۟", "translit": "۟āٓwُhdَhkَّtٱ", "root": "اخذ", "latinTranslit": "ittakhadhū"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَيْمَٰنَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَnَٰmْyَaʾ", "root": "يمن", "latinTranslit": "aymānahum"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "جُنَّةً", "translit": "ًẗَّnُjg", "root": "جنن", "latinTranslit": "junnatan"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "فَصَدُّوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُّdَṣَf", "root": "صدد", "latinTranslit": "faṣaddū"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "عَن", "translit": "nَع", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "ʿan"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "سَبِيلِ", "translit": "ِlyِbَs", "root": "سبل", "latinTranslit": "sabīli"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله", "latinTranslit": "l-lahi"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "إِنَّهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَّnِiʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "innahum"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "سَآءَ", "translit": "َءٓāَs", "root": "سوا", "latinTranslit": "sāa"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "mā"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "كَانُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُnāَk", "root": "كون", "latinTranslit": "kānū"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "يَعْمَلُونَ", "translit": "َnwُlَmْعَy", "root": "عمل", "latinTranslit": "yaʿmalūna"}], "hasIhya": false, "haleemTranslation": "they use their oaths as a cover and so bar others from God’s way: what they have been doing is truly evil––", "clearyTranslation": "they use their oaths as a cover and so bar others from God’s way: what they have been doing is truly evil––"}, {"ayah": 3, "text": "ذَٰلِكَ بِأَنَّهُمْ ءَامَنُوا۟ ثُمَّ كَفَرُوا۟ فَطُبِعَ عَلَىٰ قُلُوبِهِمْ فَهُمْ لَا يَفْقَهُونَ ", "translation": "That is because they believed, and then they disbelieved; so their hearts were sealed over, and they do not understand.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "ذَٰلِكَ", "translit": "َkِlَٰhd", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "dhālika"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "بِأَنَّهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَّnَaʾِb", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "bi-annahum"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ءَامَنُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُnَmāَء", "root": "امن", "latinTranslit": "āmanū"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ثُمَّ", "translit": "َّmُht", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "thumma"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "كَفَرُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُrَfَk", "root": "كفر", "latinTranslit": "kafarū"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "فَطُبِعَ", "translit": "َعِbُṭَf", "root": "طبع", "latinTranslit": "faṭubiʿa"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "عَلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlَع", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "ʿalā"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "قُلُوبِهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhِbwُlُq", "root": "قلب", "latinTranslit": "qulūbihim"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "فَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَf", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "fahum"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "لَا", "translit": "āَl", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "lā"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "يَفْقَهُونَ", "translit": "َnwُhَqْfَy", "root": "فقه", "latinTranslit": "yafqahūna"}], "hasIhya": false, "haleemTranslation": "because they professed faith and then rejected it, so their hearts have been sealed and they do not understand", "clearyTranslation": "because they professed faith and then rejected it, so their hearts have been sealed and they do not understand"}, {"ayah": 4, "text": "وَإِذَا رَأَيْتَهُمْ تُعْجِبُكَ أَجْسَامُهُمْۖ وَإِن يَقُولُوا۟ تَسْمَعْ لِقَوْلِهِمْۖ كَأَنَّهُمْ خُشُبٌ مُّسَنَّدَةٌۖ يَحْسَبُونَ كُلَّ صَيْحَةٍ عَلَيْهِمْۚ هُمُ ٱلْعَدُوُّ فَٱحْذَرْهُمْۚ قَٰتَلَهُمُ ٱللَّهُۖ أَنَّىٰ يُؤْفَكُونَ ", "translation": "And when you see them, their forms please you, and if they speak, you listen to their speech. [They are] as if they were pieces of wood propped up[1] - they think that every shout is against them. They are the enemy, so beware of them. May Allāh destroy them; how are they deluded?", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَإِذَا", "translit": "āَhdِiʾَw", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "wa-idhā"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "رَأَيْتَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَtْyَaʾَr", "root": "راي", "latinTranslit": "ra-aytahum"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "تُعْجِبُكَ", "translit": "َkُbِjgْعُt", "root": "عجب", "latinTranslit": "tuʿ'jibuka"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "أَجْسَامُهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhُmāَsْjgَaʾ", "root": "جسم", "latinTranslit": "ajsāmuhum"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "وَإِن", "translit": "nِiʾَw", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "wa-in"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "يَقُولُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlwُqَy", "root": "قول", "latinTranslit": "yaqūlū"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "تَسْمَعْ", "translit": "ْعَmْsَt", "root": "سمع", "latinTranslit": "tasmaʿ"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "لِقَوْلِهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhِlْwَqِl", "root": "قول", "latinTranslit": "liqawlihim"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "كَأَنَّهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَّnَaʾَk", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "ka-annahum"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "خُشُبٌ", "translit": "ٌbُhsُhk", "root": "خشب", "latinTranslit": "khushubun"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "مُّسَنَّدَةٌ", "translit": "ٌẗَdَّnَsُّm", "root": "سند", "latinTranslit": "musannadatun"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "يَحْسَبُونَ", "translit": "َnwُbَsْḥَy", "root": "حسب", "latinTranslit": "yaḥsabūna"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "كُلَّ", "translit": "َّlُk", "root": "كلل", "latinTranslit": "kulla"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "صَيْحَةٍ", "translit": "ٍẗَḥْyَṣ", "root": "صيح", "latinTranslit": "ṣayḥatin"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "عَلَيْهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhْyَlَع", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "ʿalayhim"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "هُمُ", "translit": "ُmُh", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "humu"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "ٱلْعَدُوُّ", "translit": "ُّwُdَعْlٱ", "root": "عدو", "latinTranslit": "l-ʿaduwu"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "فَٱحْذَرْهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhْrَhdْḥٱَf", "root": "حذر", "latinTranslit": "fa-iḥ'dharhum"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "قَٰتَلَهُمُ", "translit": "ُmُhَlَtَٰq", "root": "قتل", "latinTranslit": "qātalahumu"}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "ٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱ", "root": "اله", "latinTranslit": "l-lahu"}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "أَنَّىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَّnَaʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "annā"}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "يُؤْفَكُونَ", "translit": "َnwُkَfْwʾُy", "root": "افك", "latinTranslit": "yu'fakūna"}], "hasIhya": true, "haleemTranslation": "When you see them [Prophet], their outward appearance pleases you; when they speak, you listen to what they say. But they are like propped-up tim-bers––they think every cry they hear is against them––and they are the enemy. Beware of them. May God confound them! How devious they are", "clearyTranslation": "When you see them [Prophet], their outward appearance pleases you; when they speak, you listen to what they say. But they are like propped-up tim-bers––they think every cry they hear is against them––and they are the enemy. Beware of them. May God confound them! How devious they are"}, {"ayah": 5, "text": "وَإِذَا قِيلَ لَهُمْ تَعَالَوْا۟ يَسْتَغْفِرْ لَكُمْ رَسُولُ ٱللَّهِ لَوَّوْا۟ رُءُوسَهُمْ وَرَأَيْتَهُمْ يَصُدُّونَ وَهُم مُّسْتَكْبِرُونَ ", "translation": "And when it is said to them, \"Come, the Messenger of Allāh will ask forgiveness for you,\" they turn their heads aside and you see them evading while they are arrogant.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَإِذَا", "translit": "āَhdِiʾَw", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "wa-idhā"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "قِيلَ", "translit": "َlyِq", "root": "قول", "latinTranslit": "qīla"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَl", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "lahum"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "تَعَالَوْا۟", "translit": "۟āْwَlāَعَt", "root": "علو", "latinTranslit": "taʿālaw"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "يَسْتَغْفِرْ", "translit": "ْrِfْغَtْsَy", "root": "غفر", "latinTranslit": "yastaghfir"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "لَكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَl", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "lakum"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "رَسُولُ", "translit": "ُlwُsَr", "root": "رسل", "latinTranslit": "rasūlu"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله", "latinTranslit": "l-lahi"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "لَوَّوْا۟", "translit": "۟āْwَّwَl", "root": "لوي", "latinTranslit": "lawwaw"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "رُءُوسَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَswُءُr", "root": "راس", "latinTranslit": "ruūsahum"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "وَرَأَيْتَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَtْyَaʾَrَw", "root": "راي", "latinTranslit": "wara-aytahum"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "يَصُدُّونَ", "translit": "َnwُّdُṣَy", "root": "صدد", "latinTranslit": "yaṣuddūna"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "وَهُم", "translit": "mُhَw", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "wahum"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "مُّسْتَكْبِرُونَ", "translit": "َnwُrِbْkَtْsُّm", "root": "كبر", "latinTranslit": "mus'takbirūna"}], "hasIhya": false, "haleemTranslation": "They turn their heads away in disdain when they are told, ‘Come, so that the Messenger of God may ask forgiveness for you,’ and you see them walking away arrogantly", "clearyTranslation": "They turn their heads away in disdain when they are told, ‘Come, so that the Messenger of God may ask forgiveness for you,’ and you see them walking away arrogantly"}, {"ayah": 6, "text": "سَوَآءٌ عَلَيْهِمْ أَسْتَغْفَرْتَ لَهُمْ أَمْ لَمْ تَسْتَغْفِرْ لَهُمْ لَن يَغْفِرَ ٱللَّهُ لَهُمْۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ لَا يَهْدِى ٱلْقَوْمَ ٱلْفَٰسِقِينَ ", "translation": "It is all the same for them whether you ask forgiveness for them or do not ask forgiveness for them; never will Allāh forgive them. Indeed, Allāh does not guide the defiantly disobedient people.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "سَوَآءٌ", "translit": "ٌءٓāَwَs", "root": "سوي", "latinTranslit": "sawāon"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "عَلَيْهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhْyَlَع", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "ʿalayhim"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "أَسْتَغْفَرْتَ", "translit": "َtْrَfْغَtْsَaʾ", "root": "غفر", "latinTranslit": "astaghfarta"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَl", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "lahum"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "أَمْ", "translit": "ْmَaʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "am"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "لَمْ", "translit": "ْmَl", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "lam"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "تَسْتَغْفِرْ", "translit": "ْrِfْغَtْsَt", "root": "غفر", "latinTranslit": "tastaghfir"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "لَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَl", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "lahum"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "لَن", "translit": "nَl", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "lan"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "يَغْفِرَ", "translit": "َrِfْغَy", "root": "غفر", "latinTranslit": "yaghfira"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "ٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱ", "root": "اله", "latinTranslit": "l-lahu"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "لَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَl", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "lahum"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "إِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "inna"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "ٱللَّهَ", "translit": "َhَّllٱ", "root": "اله", "latinTranslit": "l-laha"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "لَا", "translit": "āَl", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "lā"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "يَهْدِى", "translit": "àِdْhَy", "root": "هدي", "latinTranslit": "yahdī"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "ٱلْقَوْمَ", "translit": "َmْwَqْlٱ", "root": "قوم", "latinTranslit": "l-qawma"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "ٱلْفَٰسِقِينَ", "translit": "َnyِqِsَٰfْlٱ", "root": "فسق", "latinTranslit": "l-fāsiqīna"}], "hasIhya": false, "haleemTranslation": "It makes no difference whether you ask forgiveness for them or not, God will not forgive them: God does not guide such treacherous people", "clearyTranslation": "It makes no difference whether you ask forgiveness for them or not, God will not forgive them: God does not guide such treacherous people"}, {"ayah": 7, "text": "هُمُ ٱلَّذِينَ يَقُولُونَ لَا تُنفِقُوا۟ عَلَىٰ مَنْ عِندَ رَسُولِ ٱللَّهِ حَتَّىٰ يَنفَضُّوا۟ۗ وَلِلَّهِ خَزَآئِنُ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلْأَرْضِ وَلَٰكِنَّ ٱلْمُنَٰفِقِينَ لَا يَفْقَهُونَ ", "translation": "They are the ones who say, \"Do not spend on those who are with the Messenger of Allāh until they disband.\" And to Allāh belong the depositories of the heavens and the earth, but the hypocrites do not understand.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "هُمُ", "translit": "ُmُh", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "humu"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "alladhīna"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "يَقُولُونَ", "translit": "َnwُlwُqَy", "root": "قول", "latinTranslit": "yaqūlūna"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لَا", "translit": "āَl", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "lā"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "تُنفِقُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُqِfnُt", "root": "نفق", "latinTranslit": "tunfiqū"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "عَلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlَع", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "ʿalā"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "مَنْ", "translit": "ْnَm", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "man"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "عِندَ", "translit": "َdnِع", "root": "عند", "latinTranslit": "ʿinda"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "رَسُولِ", "translit": "ِlwُsَr", "root": "رسل", "latinTranslit": "rasūli"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله", "latinTranslit": "l-lahi"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "حَتَّىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَّtَḥ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "ḥattā"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "يَنفَضُّوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُّḍَfnَy", "root": "فضض", "latinTranslit": "yanfaḍḍū"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "وَلِلَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّlِlَw", "root": "اله", "latinTranslit": "walillahi"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "خَزَآئِنُ", "translit": "ُnِyʾٓāَzَhk", "root": "خزن", "latinTranslit": "khazāinu"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ", "translit": "ِtَٰwَٰmَّslٱ", "root": "سمو", "latinTranslit": "l-samāwāti"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "وَٱلْأَرْضِ", "translit": "ِḍْrَaʾْlٱَw", "root": "ارض", "latinTranslit": "wal-arḍi"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "وَلَٰكِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِkَٰlَw", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "walākinna"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "ٱلْمُنَٰفِقِينَ", "translit": "َnyِqِfَٰnُmْlٱ", "root": "نفق", "latinTranslit": "l-munāfiqīna"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "لَا", "translit": "āَl", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "lā"}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "يَفْقَهُونَ", "translit": "َnwُhَqْfَy", "root": "فقه", "latinTranslit": "yafqahūna"}], "hasIhya": true, "haleemTranslation": "They are the ones who say, ‘Give nothing to those who follow God’s Messenger, until they abandon him’, but to God belong the treasures of the heavens and earth, though the hypocrites do not understand this", "clearyTranslation": "They are the ones who say, ‘Give nothing to those who follow God’s Messenger, until they abandon him’, but to God belong the treasures of the heavens and earth, though the hypocrites do not understand this"}, {"ayah": 8, "text": "يَقُولُونَ لَئِن رَّجَعْنَآ إِلَى ٱلْمَدِينَةِ لَيُخْرِجَنَّ ٱلْأَعَزُّ مِنْهَا ٱلْأَذَلَّۚ وَلِلَّهِ ٱلْعِزَّةُ وَلِرَسُولِهِۦ وَلِلْمُؤْمِنِينَ وَلَٰكِنَّ ٱلْمُنَٰفِقِينَ لَا يَعْلَمُونَ ", "translation": "They say, \"If we return to al-Madīnah, the more honored [for power] will surely expel therefrom the more humble.\" And to Allāh belongs [all] honor, and to His Messenger, and to the believers, but the hypocrites do not know.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "يَقُولُونَ", "translit": "َnwُlwُqَy", "root": "قول", "latinTranslit": "yaqūlūna"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لَئِن", "translit": "nِyʾَl", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "la-in"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "رَّجَعْنَآ", "translit": "ٓāَnْعَjgَّr", "root": "رجع", "latinTranslit": "rajaʿnā"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "إِلَى", "translit": "àَlِiʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "ilā"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلْمَدِينَةِ", "translit": "ِẗَnyِdَmْlٱ", "root": "مدن", "latinTranslit": "l-madīnati"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "لَيُخْرِجَنَّ", "translit": "َّnَjgِrْhkُyَl", "root": "خرج", "latinTranslit": "layukh'rijanna"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "ٱلْأَعَزُّ", "translit": "ُّzَعَaʾْlٱ", "root": "عزز", "latinTranslit": "l-aʿazu"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "مِنْهَا", "translit": "āَhْnِm", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "min'hā"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "ٱلْأَذَلَّ", "translit": "َّlَhdَaʾْlٱ", "root": "ذلل", "latinTranslit": "l-adhala"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "وَلِلَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّlِlَw", "root": "اله", "latinTranslit": "walillahi"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "ٱلْعِزَّةُ", "translit": "ُẗَّzِعْlٱ", "root": "عزز", "latinTranslit": "l-ʿizatu"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "وَلِرَسُولِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِlwُsَrِlَw", "root": "رسل", "latinTranslit": "walirasūlihi"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "وَلِلْمُؤْمِنِينَ", "translit": "َnyِnِmْwʾُmْlِlَw", "root": "امن", "latinTranslit": "walil'mu'minīna"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "وَلَٰكِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِkَٰlَw", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "walākinna"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "ٱلْمُنَٰفِقِينَ", "translit": "َnyِqِfَٰnُmْlٱ", "root": "نفق", "latinTranslit": "l-munāfiqīna"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "لَا", "translit": "āَl", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "lā"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "يَعْلَمُونَ", "translit": "َnwُmَlْعَy", "root": "علم", "latinTranslit": "yaʿlamūna"}], "hasIhya": false, "haleemTranslation": "They say, ‘Once we return to Medina the powerful will drive out the weak,’ but power belongs to God, to His Messenger, and to the believers, though the hypocrites do not know this", "clearyTranslation": "They say, ‘Once we return to Medina the powerful will drive out the weak,’ but power belongs to God, to His Messenger, and to the believers, though the hypocrites do not know this"}, {"ayah": 9, "text": "يَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ لَا تُلْهِكُمْ أَمْوَٰلُكُمْ وَلَآ أَوْلَٰدُكُمْ عَن ذِكْرِ ٱللَّهِۚ وَمَن يَفْعَلْ ذَٰلِكَ فَأُو۟لَٰٓئِكَ هُمُ ٱلْخَٰسِرُونَ ", "translation": "O you who have believed, let not your wealth and your children divert you from the remembrance of Allāh. And whoever does that - then those are the losers.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "يَٰٓأَيُّهَا", "translit": "āَhُّyَaʾَٰٓy", "root": "ايي", "latinTranslit": "yāayyuhā"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "alladhīna"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ءَامَنُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُnَmāَء", "root": "امن", "latinTranslit": "āmanū"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لَا", "translit": "āَl", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "lā"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "تُلْهِكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkِhْlُt", "root": "لهو", "latinTranslit": "tul'hikum"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "أَمْوَٰلُكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkُlَٰwْmَaʾ", "root": "مول", "latinTranslit": "amwālukum"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "وَلَآ", "translit": "ٓāَlَw", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "walā"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "أَوْلَٰدُكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkُdَٰlْwَaʾ", "root": "ولد", "latinTranslit": "awlādukum"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "عَن", "translit": "nَع", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "ʿan"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "ذِكْرِ", "translit": "ِrْkِhd", "root": "ذكر", "latinTranslit": "dhik'ri"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله", "latinTranslit": "l-lahi"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "وَمَن", "translit": "nَmَw", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "waman"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "يَفْعَلْ", "translit": "ْlَعْfَy", "root": "فعل", "latinTranslit": "yafʿal"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "ذَٰلِكَ", "translit": "َkِlَٰhd", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "dhālika"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "فَأُو۟لَٰٓئِكَ", "translit": "َkِyʾَٰٓl۟wُaʾَf", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "fa-ulāika"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "هُمُ", "translit": "ُmُh", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "humu"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "ٱلْخَٰسِرُونَ", "translit": "َnwُrِsَٰhkْlٱ", "root": "خسر", "latinTranslit": "l-khāsirūna"}], "hasIhya": true, "haleemTranslation": "Believers, do not let your wealth and your children distract you from remembering God: those who do so will be the ones who lose", "clearyTranslation": "Believers, do not let your wealth and your children distract you from remembering God: those who do so will be the ones who lose"}, {"ayah": 10, "text": "وَأَنفِقُوا۟ مِن مَّا رَزَقْنَٰكُم مِّن قَبْلِ أَن يَأْتِىَ أَحَدَكُمُ ٱلْمَوْتُ فَيَقُولَ رَبِّ لَوْلَآ أَخَّرْتَنِىٓ إِلَىٰٓ أَجَلٍ قَرِيبٍ فَأَصَّدَّقَ وَأَكُن مِّنَ ٱلصَّٰلِحِينَ ", "translation": "And spend [in the way of Allāh] from what We have provided you before death approaches one of you and he says, \"My Lord, if only You would delay me for a brief term so I would give charity and be of the righteous.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَأَنفِقُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُqِfnَaʾَw", "root": "نفق", "latinTranslit": "wa-anfiqū"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "min"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مَّا", "translit": "āَّm", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "mā"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "رَزَقْنَٰكُم", "translit": "mُkَٰnْqَzَr", "root": "رزق", "latinTranslit": "razaqnākum"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مِّن", "translit": "nِّm", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "min"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "قَبْلِ", "translit": "ِlْbَq", "root": "قبل", "latinTranslit": "qabli"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "أَن", "translit": "nَaʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "an"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "يَأْتِىَ", "translit": "َàِtْaʾَy", "root": "اتي", "latinTranslit": "yatiya"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "أَحَدَكُمُ", "translit": "ُmُkَdَḥَaʾ", "root": "احد", "latinTranslit": "aḥadakumu"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "ٱلْمَوْتُ", "translit": "ُtْwَmْlٱ", "root": "موت", "latinTranslit": "l-mawtu"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "فَيَقُولَ", "translit": "َlwُqَyَf", "root": "قول", "latinTranslit": "fayaqūla"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "رَبِّ", "translit": "ِّbَr", "root": "ربب", "latinTranslit": "rabbi"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "لَوْلَآ", "translit": "ٓāَlْwَl", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "lawlā"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "أَخَّرْتَنِىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِnَtْrَّhkَaʾ", "root": "اخر", "latinTranslit": "akhartanī"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "إِلَىٰٓ", "translit": "ٰٓàَlِiʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "ilā"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "أَجَلٍ", "translit": "ٍlَjgَaʾ", "root": "اجل", "latinTranslit": "ajalin"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "قَرِيبٍ", "translit": "ٍbyِrَq", "root": "قرب", "latinTranslit": "qarībin"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "فَأَصَّدَّقَ", "translit": "َqَّdَّṣَaʾَf", "root": "صدق", "latinTranslit": "fa-aṣṣaddaqa"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "وَأَكُن", "translit": "nُkَaʾَw", "root": "كون", "latinTranslit": "wa-akun"}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "مِّنَ", "translit": "َnِّm", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "mina"}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "ٱلصَّٰلِحِينَ", "translit": "َnyِḥِlَّٰṣlٱ", "root": "صلح", "latinTranslit": "l-ṣāliḥīna"}], "hasIhya": false, "haleemTranslation": "Give out of what We have provided for you, before death comes to one of you and he says, ‘My Lord, if You would only reprieve me for a little while, I would give in charity and become one of the righteous.’", "clearyTranslation": "Give out of what We have provided for you, before death comes to one of you and he says, ‘My Lord, if You would only reprieve me for a little while, I would give in charity and become one of the righteous.’"}, {"ayah": 11, "text": "وَلَن يُؤَخِّرَ ٱللَّهُ نَفْسًا إِذَا جَآءَ أَجَلُهَاۚ وَٱللَّهُ خَبِيرٌۢ بِمَا تَعْمَلُونَ ", "translation": "But never will Allāh delay a soul when its time has come. And Allāh is Aware of what you do.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَلَن", "translit": "nَlَw", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "walan"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يُؤَخِّرَ", "translit": "َrِّhkَwʾُy", "root": "اخر", "latinTranslit": "yu-akhira"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱ", "root": "اله", "latinTranslit": "l-lahu"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "نَفْسًا", "translit": "āًsْfَn", "root": "نفس", "latinTranslit": "nafsan"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "إِذَا", "translit": "āَhdِiʾ", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "idhā"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "جَآءَ", "translit": "َءٓāَjg", "root": "جيا", "latinTranslit": "jāa"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "أَجَلُهَا", "translit": "āَhُlَjgَaʾ", "root": "اجل", "latinTranslit": "ajaluhā"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "وَٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱَw", "root": "اله", "latinTranslit": "wal-lahu"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "خَبِيرٌۢ", "translit": "ٌۢryِbَhk", "root": "خبر", "latinTranslit": "khabīrun"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "بِمَا", "translit": "āَmِb", "root": "", "latinTranslit": "bimā"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "تَعْمَلُونَ", "translit": "َnwُlَmْعَt", "root": "عمل", "latinTranslit": "taʿmalūna"}], "hasIhya": false, "haleemTranslation": "God does not reprieve a soul when its turn comes: God is fully aware of what you do", "clearyTranslation": "God does not reprieve a soul when its turn comes: God is fully aware of what you do"}], "tafsir": {"1": [{"arabic": "الإسلام وهو الذي ذكره الله تعالى في كتابه في مواضع شتى كقوله عز وجل {إذا جاءك المنافقون قالوا نشهد إنك لرسول الله والله يعلم إنك لرسوله والله يشهد إن المنافقين لكاذبون} أي في دلالتهم بقولهم على ضمائرهم وقال تعالى {ومن الناس من يعجبك قوله في الحياة الدنيا ويشهد الله على ما في قلبه وهو ألد الخصام وإذا تولى سعى في الأرض ليفسد فيها} الآية وقال تعالى {وإذا لقوكم قالوا آمنا وإذا خلوا عضوا عليكم الأنامل من الغيظ} وقال تعالى {يراؤون الناس ولا يذكرون الله إلا قليلا مذبذبين بين ذلك} والآيات فيهم كثيرة وكان النفاق يكثر في ابتداء الإسلام ممن يدخل في ظاهر الإسلام ابتداء لغرض وذل", "english": "The first degree: ostentation in the very root of faith (asl al-iman). And this is the gravest of the gates of ostentation, and its practitioner is eternally abiding in the Fire (mukhallad fi al-nar). He is the one who outwardly utters the two words of the testimony (kalimata al-shahadah) while his inward being is crammed with denial (al-takdhib); yet he ostentatiously displays the outward form of Islam. And he is the one whom God the Exalted mentioned in His Book in numerous places, such as His saying — Mighty and Majestic is He: {«إذا جاءك المنافقون قالوا نشهد إنك لرسول الله والله يعلم إنك لرسوله والله يشهد إن المنافقين لكاذبون»} — \"When the hypocrites come to you, they say: 'We bear witness that you are indeed the Messenger of God.' And God knows that you are indeed His Messenger, and God bears witness that the hypocrites are indeed liars\" — that is, liars in their indication, by their speech, of what is in their consciences. And He said the Exalted: {«ومن الناس من يعجبك قوله في الحياة الدنيا ويشهد الله على ما في قلبه وهو ألد الخصام وإذا تولى سعى في الأرض ليفسد فيها»} — \"And among mankind is he whose speech pleases you in the life of this world, and he calls God to witness what is in his heart, yet he is the most contentious of adversaries. And when he turns away, he strives throughout the land to cause corruption therein\" — the verse. And He said the Exalted: {«وإذا لقوكم قالوا آمنا وإذا خلوا عضوا عليكم الأنامل من الغيظ»} — \"And when they meet you, they say: 'We believe'; but when they are alone, they bite their fingertips at you in rage.\" And He said the Exalted: {«يراؤون الناس ولا يذكرون الله إلا قليلا مذبذبين بين ذلك»} — \"They show off to the people, and they do not remember God except a little, wavering between that\" — and the verses concerning them are many.", "book_title": "Ihya Ulum al-Din", "section_title_ar": "Section 818", "section_title_en": "On the Degrees of Ostentation in Worship — The Second Pillar: That by Which One Ostentatiously Displays (Al-Riya' bi al-Ta'at)", "section_index": 818, "anchors": "- Root: قصد (Qasada)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core meaning of \"intending, aiming toward a goal, directing one's purpose.\"\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"القصد: استقامة الطريق\" — intention as the straight path of the soul toward its object; in moral theology, it denotes the deliberate orientation of the will that determines the moral value of an act.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (Haqiqah): \"قصدته وقصدت له\" — direct aiming. Metaphorical (Majaz): \"قصد في الأمر إذا لم يجاوز فيه الحد\" — moderation; here, the \"intention\" (qasd) is the precise measure by which an act is weighed between reward and punishment.\n- Root: راءى (Ra'a) — from Root: رأى (Ra'a)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: \"الرياء: إظهار العمل ليراه الناس\" — showing one's deed so that people may see it; derived from الرؤية (sight/seeing).\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Riya' is a branch of shirk (associating partners with God), for the actor directs his deed not to God alone but to the gaze of creatures, thus dividing his intention between the Creator and creation.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: seeing with the eye. Metaphorical: \"راءى فلان\" — to perform an act for the sake of being seen, i.e., seeking the approval of onlookers rather than the sight of God.\n- Root: خلق (Khalaqa)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: \"الخلق: التقدير المستقيم\" — measuring and proportioning; also \"خلق الثوب\" — wearing out a garment until it is threadbare.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"الخلق أصله: التقدير المستقيم\" — creation as precise estimation; in moral context, the \"خلق\" (character) is the inward measure by which a soul is formed.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"خلق الخراز الأديم\" — the leather-worker cutting and measuring hide. Metaphorical: \"خلق الله الخلق: أوجده على تقدير أوجبته الحكمة\" — God's creation of creatures upon a measure required by wisdom; here, the \"creatures\" (الخلق) whose blame (المقت) is feared by the ostentatious worshipper.\n- Root: نفق (Nafaqa)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: \"نفق الشيء: مضى ونفد\" — to pass away, to be spent, to perish.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"نفق الشيء: مضى ونفد، ينفق، إما بالبيع نحو: نفق البيع نفاقا\" — to find a ready market; \"ومنها نفاق الأيم\" — hypocrisy as the \"passing\" of a false coin in the market of religion.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"نفقت الدراهم\" — coins circulating and being spent. Metaphorical: \"نافق\" — the hypocrite (munafiq) whose outward faith circulates among people while his inward disbelief is void; the ostentatious man \"spends\" his deeds on the market of human praise.\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الفصل بين الجار والمجرور (Prepositional Interposition) — The syntactic separation between a governing preposition and its object, as in \"له من الثواب مثل ما عليه من العقاب,\" where the prepositional phrases are interposed to balance two opposing clauses, mirroring the theological weighing of reward against punishment.", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's epistemic insights into the spiritual heart and inner faith, from 'Ihya Ulum al-Din'", "badge": "Insight"}, {"arabic": "يشهد إن المنافقين لكاذبون} أي في دلالتهم بقولهم على ضمائرهم وقال تعالى {ومن الناس من يعجبك قوله في الحياة الدنيا ويشهد الله على ما في قلبه وهو ألد الخصام وإذا تولى سعى في الأرض ليفسد فيها} الآية وقال تعالى {وإذا لقوكم قالوا آمنا وإذا خلوا عضوا عليكم الأنامل من الغيظ} وقال تعالى {يراؤون الناس ولا يذكرون الله إلا قليلا مذبذبين بين ذلك} والآيات فيهم كثيرة وكان النفاق يكثر في ابتداء الإسلام ممن يدخل في ظاهر الإسلام ابتداء لغرض", "english": "The first degree: ostentation in the very root of faith (asl al-iman). And this is the gravest of the gates of ostentation, and its practitioner is eternally abiding in the Fire (mukhallad fi al-nar). He is the one who outwardly utters the two words of the testimony (kalimata al-shahadah) while his inward being is crammed with denial (al-takdhib); yet he ostentatiously displays the outward form of Islam. And he is the one whom God the Exalted mentioned in His Book in numerous places, such as His saying — Mighty and Majestic is He: {«إذا جاءك المنافقون قالوا نشهد إنك لرسول الله والله يعلم إنك لرسوله والله يشهد إن المنافقين لكاذبون»} — \"When the hypocrites come to you, they say: 'We bear witness that you are indeed the Messenger of God.' And God knows that you are indeed His Messenger, and God bears witness that the hypocrites are indeed liars\" — that is, liars in their indication, by their speech, of what is in their consciences. And He said the Exalted: {«ومن الناس من يعجبك قوله في الحياة الدنيا ويشهد الله على ما في قلبه وهو ألد الخصام وإذا تولى سعى في الأرض ليفسد فيها»} — \"And among mankind is he whose speech pleases you in the life of this world, and he calls God to witness what is in his heart, yet he is the most contentious of adversaries. And when he turns away, he strives throughout the land to cause corruption therein\" — the verse. And He said the Exalted: {«وإذا لقوكم قالوا آمنا وإذا خلوا عضوا عليكم الأنامل من الغيظ»} — \"And when they meet you, they say: 'We believe'; but when they are alone, they bite their fingertips at you in rage.\" And He said the Exalted: {«يراؤون الناس ولا يذكرون الله إلا قليلا مذبذبين بين ذلك»} — \"They show off to the people, and they do not remember God except a little, wavering between that\" — and the verses concerning them are many.", "book_title": "Ihya Ulum al-Din", "section_title_ar": "Section 818", "section_title_en": "On the Degrees of Ostentation in Worship — The Second Pillar: That by Which One Ostentatiously Displays (Al-Riya' bi al-Ta'at)", "section_index": 818, "anchors": "- Root: قصد (Qasada)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core meaning of \"intending, aiming toward a goal, directing one's purpose.\"\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"القصد: استقامة الطريق\" — intention as the straight path of the soul toward its object; in moral theology, it denotes the deliberate orientation of the will that determines the moral value of an act.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (Haqiqah): \"قصدته وقصدت له\" — direct aiming. Metaphorical (Majaz): \"قصد في الأمر إذا لم يجاوز فيه الحد\" — moderation; here, the \"intention\" (qasd) is the precise measure by which an act is weighed between reward and punishment.\n- Root: راءى (Ra'a) — from Root: رأى (Ra'a)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: \"الرياء: إظهار العمل ليراه الناس\" — showing one's deed so that people may see it; derived from الرؤية (sight/seeing).\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Riya' is a branch of shirk (associating partners with God), for the actor directs his deed not to God alone but to the gaze of creatures, thus dividing his intention between the Creator and creation.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: seeing with the eye. Metaphorical: \"راءى فلان\" — to perform an act for the sake of being seen, i.e., seeking the approval of onlookers rather than the sight of God.\n- Root: خلق (Khalaqa)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: \"الخلق: التقدير المستقيم\" — measuring and proportioning; also \"خلق الثوب\" — wearing out a garment until it is threadbare.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"الخلق أصله: التقدير المستقيم\" — creation as precise estimation; in moral context, the \"خلق\" (character) is the inward measure by which a soul is formed.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"خلق الخراز الأديم\" — the leather-worker cutting and measuring hide. Metaphorical: \"خلق الله الخلق: أوجده على تقدير أوجبته الحكمة\" — God's creation of creatures upon a measure required by wisdom; here, the \"creatures\" (الخلق) whose blame (المقت) is feared by the ostentatious worshipper.\n- Root: نفق (Nafaqa)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: \"نفق الشيء: مضى ونفد\" — to pass away, to be spent, to perish.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"نفق الشيء: مضى ونفد، ينفق، إما بالبيع نحو: نفق البيع نفاقا\" — to find a ready market; \"ومنها نفاق الأيم\" — hypocrisy as the \"passing\" of a false coin in the market of religion.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"نفقت الدراهم\" — coins circulating and being spent. Metaphorical: \"نافق\" — the hypocrite (munafiq) whose outward faith circulates among people while his inward disbelief is void; the ostentatious man \"spends\" his deeds on the market of human praise.\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الفصل بين الجار والمجرور (Prepositional Interposition) — The syntactic separation between a governing preposition and its object, as in \"له من الثواب مثل ما عليه من العقاب,\" where the prepositional phrases are interposed to balance two opposing clauses, mirroring the theological weighing of reward against punishment.", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's epistemic insights into the spiritual heart and inner faith, from 'Ihya Ulum al-Din'", "badge": "Insight"}], "4": [{"arabic": "على أمر {يحسبون كل صيحة عليهم هم العدو فاحذرهم} وقد اشتد حرصهم على الدنيا فلا يظنون بغيرهم إلا الحرص عليها قال المتنبي إذا ساء فعل المرء ساءت ظنونه ...", "english": "There is no doubt that whoever mixes with people and shares in their affairs is never free from an envier and an enemy who thinks evil of him and imagines that he is preparing for hostilities against him, laying snares against him, and secretly plotting harm behind his back. For people, however intense their greed for a matter, {«يَحْسَبُونَ كُلَّ صَيْحَةٍ عَلَيْهِمْ ۚ هُمُ الْعَدُوُّ فَاحْذَرْهُمْ»} (\"They think every cry is against them. They are the enemy, so beware of them\") — and their greed for the world is intense, so they do not suspect others of anything but greed for it.", "book_title": "Ihya Ulum al-Din", "section_title_ar": "Section 454", "section_title_en": "The Book of Seclusion (Kitāb al-ʿUzlah) — Section 454: The Harms of Social Mixing and the Wisdom of Withdrawal", "section_index": 454, "anchors": "- Root: جمع (j-m-ʿ)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: To gather, assemble, bring together; the core sense of drawing things near one another.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Theological nuance of communal gathering (ijtimāʿ) as the arena where envy, hypocrisy, and mutual harm are generated; contrasted with the spiritual safety of solitary withdrawal.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (ḥaqīqah) — physical assembly of people; Metaphorical (majāz) — the \"gathering\" of hidden grudges and stored grievances against a person, as in \"أمر بني فلان بجمع\" (a concealed matter).\n- Root: ظهر (ẓ-h-r)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: The back; to appear, become manifest.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Used metaphorically for bearing burdens — sins weigh upon the back; here, the \"back\" of a camel or horse is the vehicle of transport that the wicked \"break\" (ʿaqarū) through misuse, symbolizing how evil companions destroy what carries them.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal — the physical back of a riding beast; Metaphorical — \"قلبت الأمر ظهرًا لبطن\" (turning a matter over), and the notion of people being \"mounted\" upon one's trust, only to betray it.\n- Root: وقد (w-q-d)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: To kindle, ignite a fire; fuel.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Fire that burns with intense heat; here, the \"fire\" of slander (ghībah), envy, and malice that evil companions kindle against the believer.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal — kindling a physical fire; Metaphorical — \"وقد الحصى\" (the pebbles became scorching hot), i.e., the burning intensity of hostility; \"قلب وقاد\" (a blazing heart) — the inflamed passions of the envious.\n- Root: شعر (sh-ʿ-r)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Hair; to perceive with acute sensitivity.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"شعرت كذا\" — to know something with the precision of touching a hair; the poet (shāʿir) is so named for his fine perception. Here, the believer's fear: \"خشيت أن أسلب ديني ولا أشعر\" — that his religion might be stripped away without his even perceiving it, due to the subtle, imperceptible corruption of character by evil companions.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal — bodily hair; Metaphorical — \"استشعر خوفًا\" (he felt a deep-seated fear), i.e., the internalization of harmful traits from bad company without conscious awareness.\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الفصل بين الجار والمجرور (Prepositional Interposition) — The permissibility of separating a preposition from its governed noun when the intervening element is semantically complete, allowing for rhetorical emphasis and the insertion of parenthetical warnings, as in the structure of the Prophet's saying and the aphorisms cited herein.", "content_type": "general", "topic": "Classical commentary from Al-Ghazali's Ihya Ulum al-Din, from 'Ihya Ulum al-Din'", "badge": "Commentary"}], "7": [{"arabic": "الله الرزق واعبدوه وقال عز وجل ولله خزائن السموات والأرض ولكن المنافقين لا يفقهون وقال عز وجل يدبر الأمر ما من شفيع إلا من بعد إذنه وكل ما ذكر في القرآن من التوحيد فهو تنبيه على قطع الملاحظة عن الأغيار والتوكل على الواحد القهار وأما الأخبار فقد قال صلى الله عليه وسلم فيما رواه ابن مسعود أريت الأمم في الموسم فرأيت أمتي قد ملأوا السهل والجبل فأعجبتني كثرتهم وهيأتهم فقيل لي أرضيت قلت نعم قيل ومع هؤلاء سبعون ألفا يدخلون الجنة بغير حساب قيل من هم يا رسول الله قال الذين لا يكتوون ولا", "english": "And He, exalted is He, said: {إِنَّ الَّذِينَ تَعْبُدُونَ مِن دُونِ اللَّهِ لَا يَمْلِكُونَ لَكُمْ رِزْقًا فَابْتَغُوا عِندَ اللَّهِ الرِّزْقَ وَاعْبُدُوهُ} — \"Indeed, those you worship besides Allah do not possess for you any provision, so seek provision from Allah and worship Him.\" And He, mighty and majestic, said: {وَلِلَّهِ خَزَائِنُ السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالْأَرْضِ وَلَٰكِنَّ الْمُنَافِقِينَ لَا يَفْقَهُونَ} — \"And to Allah belong the treasuries of the heavens and the earth, but the hypocrites do not understand.\" And He, mighty and majestic, said: {يُدَبِّرُ الْأَمْرَ مَا مِن شَفِيعٍ إِلَّا مِن بَعْدِ إِذْنِهِ} — \"He manages the affair; there is no intercessor except after His permission.\" And everything mentioned in the Qur'an concerning divine unity (tawḥīd) is an alert to severing the regard for other-than-Allah (al-aghyār) and relying solely upon the One, the Subduer (al-Wāḥid al-Qahhār).", "book_title": "Ihya Ulum al-Din", "section_title_ar": "Section 1103", "section_title_en": "Section 1103 — On the First Part Concerning Divine Unity (Tawḥīd) and the Perfection of Trust in Allah", "section_index": 1103, "anchors": "- Root: وكل (W-K-L)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core meaning of delegating, entrusting, and appointing another as a deputy or guardian over one's affairs.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"التوكيل: أن تعتمد على غيرك وتجعله نائبا عنك\" — Trust (tawakkul) is to rely upon another and make him a deputy; the true Wakīl is Allah alone, as in {وَكَفَىٰ بِاللَّهِ وَكِيلًا}.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (ḥaqīqah): \"توكل على الله ولا تتكل على غيره\" — reliance on Allah. Metaphorical (majāz): \"وكل همه بكذا\" — one who delegates his care to a thing, implying abandonment by Allah of those who turn to other than Him.\n- Root: عبد (ʿ-B-D)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Servitude, submission, and humble obedience; the created being as subjugated servant.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"العبودية: إظهار التذلل، والعبادة أبلغ منها\" — servitude is the display of humility; worship is its utmost degree, due only to Allah. All besides Allah are \"عباد أمثالكم\" — servants like yourselves, incapable of independent provision.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"عبد بين العبودية\" — a slave bound in servitude. Metaphorical: \"استعبده الطمع\" — greed enslaves a man, just as reliance on creatures enslaves the heart.\n- Root: رسل (R-S-L)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Sending forth with ease and gentleness; a messenger dispatched with a message.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"أصل الرسل: الانبعاث على التؤدة\" — the root is gentle dispatch; the messenger is one sent, and the verse {وَأْمُرْ أَهْلَكَ بِالصَّلَاةِ} is a divine sending of command.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"أرسل الله في الأمم رسلا\" — Allah sent messengers to nations. Metaphorical: \"أرسل الله عليهم العذاب\" — Allah loosed punishment upon them, showing His sole agency.\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الفصل بين الجار والمجرور (Prepositional Interposition) — The rule governing the separation of the preposition from its object for rhetorical emphasis, as in \"على ربهم يتوكلون\" where the preposition \"على\" is fronted before its governed noun \"ربهم\" to highlight exclusive reliance, a construction permissible when the clause is semantically complete and the fronting serves emphasis (takhrīṣ).", "content_type": "hadith", "topic": "Prophetic traditions and scholastic commentary by Al-Ghazali, from 'Ihya Ulum al-Din'", "badge": "Hadith"}], "9": [{"arabic": "وقد قال الله تعالى يا أيها الذين آمنوا أنفقوا من طيبات ما كسبتم ومما أخرجنا لكم من الأرض ولا تيمموا الخبيث منه تنفقون ولستم بآخذيه إلا أن تغمضوا فيه أي لا تأخذوه إلا مع كراهية وحياء وهو معنى الإغماض فلا تؤثروا به ربكم وفي الخبر سبق درهم مائة ألف درهم (3) وذلك بأن يخرجه الإنسان وهو من أحل ماله وأجوده فيصدر ذلك عن الرضا والفرح بالبذل وقد يخرج مائة ألف درهم مما يكره من ماله فيدل ذلك على أنه ليس يؤثر الله عز وجل بشيء مما يحبه وبذل", "english": "And in the ḥadīth of Abān, from Anas ibn Mālik — may Allah be pleased with him: \"Blessed (ṭūbā) is a servant who spends from wealth he earned without disobedience.\" And if what he puts forth is not from the finest of his wealth, then that is from ill-manners (sūʾ al-adab), since he may have kept the finest for himself, or for his servant, or for his family — and so he has preferred over Allah — Exalted is He — someone other than Him. Were he to do this with his guest and offer him the worst food in his house, that would kindle rage in his breast. This is if his regard is toward Allah — Exalted is He. And if his regard is toward himself and his reward in the Hereafter, then he is not intelligent who prefers others over himself — for he has nothing of his wealth save what he gave in charity (so it remains for him) or what he ate (so it is consumed). And what he eats is merely the satisfaction of a need in the present moment. It is not from intelligence to confine one's regard to the immediate (al-ʿājilah) and to abandon laying up provision (al-iddikhār). Allah — Exalted is He — has said: {«يا أيها الذين آمنوا أنفقوا من طيبات ما كسبتم ومما أخرجنا لكم من الأرض ولا تيمموا الخبيث منه تنفقون ولستم بآخذيه إلا أن تغمضوا فيه»} (\"O you who believe, spend from the good things you have earned and from what We have brought forth for you from the earth, and do not aim at the bad thereof to spend — while you would not take it yourselves save with closed eyes\") — that is, you would not take it save with aversion and shame, and that is the meaning of closing the eyes (al-ighmāḍ). So do not prefer over your Lord that which you yourselves would disdain.", "book_title": "Ihya Ulum al-Din", "section_title_ar": "Section 175", "section_title_en": "The Inner Conditions of Charity — Section 175 (From The Revival of the Religious Sciences, Book of the Mysteries of Almsgiving)", "section_index": 175, "anchors": "- Root: قلب (q-l-b)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: \"To turn, overturn, transform a thing from one state to another; to rotate, to flip\"\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"قلب الشيء: تصريفه وصرفه عن وجه إلى وجه\" — the heart is so named because of its constant turning and transformation between states\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"قلب الشيء قلبا: حوله عن وجهه\" (to turn a thing from its face). Metaphorical: \"رجل قلب حول: يقلب الأمور ويحتال\" — one who turns matters over and manages them; \"قلبوا لك الأمور\" (they turned matters against you)\n- Root: وجل (w-j-l)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: \"Fear, dread, apprehension that strikes the heart\"\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"الوجل: استشعار الخوف\" — the sensing of fear; cited in {«إنما المؤمنون الذين إذا ذكر الله وجلت قلوبهم»}\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"رجل وجل، وقوم وجال\" — a fearful man, a fearful people; \"وفي قلبه وجل\" — in his heart is dread\n- Root: عجب (ʿ-j-b)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: \"Wonder, amazement; self-admiration, vanity\"\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Self-admiration (al-ʿujb) is a destructive spiritual ailment that nullifies deeds\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: wonder at something extraordinary. Metaphorical: self-conceit regarding one's own acts of obedience\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الحصر والتقييد (Restriction & Focused Predication) — governing the precise limitation of general categories (al-ṣifāt al-khāṣṣah within al-aṣnāf al-thamāniyyah) and the conditional structure of acceptance\n\n---\n\n##", "content_type": "general", "topic": "Classical commentary from Al-Ghazali's Ihya Ulum al-Din, from 'Ihya Ulum al-Din'", "badge": "Commentary"}, {"arabic": "الله تعالى يا أيها الذين آمنوا لا تلهكم أموالكم ولا أولادكم عن ذكر الله ومن يفعل ذلك فأولئك هم الخاسرون وقال تعالى إنما أموالكم وأولادكم", "english": "Allah Most High said: {«يا أيها الذين آمنوا لا تلهكم أموالكم ولا أولادكم عن ذكر الله ومن يفعل ذلك فأولئك هم الخاسرون»} — \"O you who believe, let not your wealth and your children divert you from the remembrance of Allah. And whoever does that — then it is they who are the losers.\" And He said Most High: {«إنما أموالكم وأولادكم فتنة والله عنده أجر عظيم»} — \"Your wealth and your children are only a trial, and Allah — with Him is a mighty reward.\" So whoever chooses his wealth and his child over what is with Allah has indeed lost and been defrauded a tremendous loss. And He said, Mighty and Majestic: {«من كان يريد الحياة الدنيا وزينتها»} — \"Whoever desires the life of this world and its adornment...\" — to the end of the verse. And He said Most High: {«إن الإنسان ليطغى أن رآه استغنى»} — \"Indeed, man does transgress when he sees himself self-sufficient.\" There is no might and no power except through Allah, the Exalted, the Magnificent. And He said Most High: {«ألهاكم التكاثر»} — \"Vying in increase diverts you.\"", "book_title": "Ihya Ulum al-Din", "section_title_ar": "Section 753", "section_title_en": "The Revival of the Religious Sciences — Book on Poverty and Abstinence: The Blame of Wealth and Its Perils", "section_index": 753, "anchors": "- Root: لهو (l-h-w)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: To divert, distract, or occupy oneself away from a matter of greater import; amusement that turns one from serious concern.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Theologically, *lahw* denotes that which diverts the heart from Allah — the root cause of spiritual ruin, as wealth and children are here designated as distracting agents.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: play/amusement. Metaphorical: any engrossing worldly pursuit that veils one from the Hereafter.\n- Root: كثر (k-th-r)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Abundance, multitude, increase in number or quantity.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): *Takāthur* (vying in increase) is censured as the competitive accumulation of worldly goods for pride, not need.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: seeking more. Metaphorical: the obsessive race toward worldly accumulation that hardens the heart.\n- Root: غبن (gh-b-n)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: To cheat, defraud, or suffer loss in a transaction; to be outwitted.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): In the Hereafter, *ghubn* is the ultimate loss — exchanging eternal bliss for fleeting worldly gain.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: commercial deception. Metaphorical: the soul's self-deception in preferring the ephemeral over the everlasting.\n- Root: فتن (f-t-n)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Trial, tribulation, test; that which sifts the sincere from the insincere.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): *Fitnah* is a divine test through which the heart's attachment to worldly goods is exposed.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: burning in fire (as gold is refined). Metaphorical: wealth as a crucible for faith.\n- Sibawayh Rule: Restriction and Focused Predication (*Bāb al-Ḥaṣr wa al-Taqyīd bi-innamā*) — The particle *innamā* in {«إنما أموالكم وأولادكم فتنة»} restricts the predicate, affirming that wealth and children are solely a trial, not an end in themselves.", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's epistemic insights into the spiritual heart and inner faith, from 'Ihya Ulum al-Din'", "badge": "Insight"}]}, "wordTiming": {"minshawi": {"1": [[1, 10, 1141], [2, 1141, 3607], [3, 3607, 5812], [4, 5812, 8074], [5, 8074, 9001], [6, 9001, 9996], [7, 9996, 11466], [8, 11466, 12371], [9, 12371, 13819], [10, 13819, 15097], [11, 15097, 16092], [12, 16092, 17766], [13, 17766, 19214], [14, 19214, 20458], [15, 20458, 21227], [16, 21227, 23432], [17, 23432, 25310]], "63:1": [[1, 10, 1141], [2, 1141, 3607], [3, 3607, 5812], [4, 5812, 8074], [5, 8074, 9001], [6, 9001, 9996], [7, 9996, 11466], [8, 11466, 12371], [9, 12371, 13819], [10, 13819, 15097], [11, 15097, 16092], [12, 16092, 17766], [13, 17766, 19214], [14, 19214, 20458], [15, 20458, 21227], [16, 21227, 23432], [17, 23432, 25310]], "2": [[1, 520, 3061], [2, 3061, 4398], [3, 4398, 5111], [4, 5111, 6734], [5, 6734, 7135], [6, 7